# The debug flavour, on top of ps3.config: the research drivers that have no bus alias, so nothing loads
# them by itself (modprobe by hand, root only). The release kernel has neither of them (K4, round 3):
# - ps3lv1call (ps3/0250): any lv1 hypercall for root, flash and storage regions included; the
#   ps3disk write guard (local/0045) can't stop what goes through it;
# - ps3physmem (ps3/0140): all of the partition's memory mapped into userspace.
# PS3_DISP_MANAGER (ps3/0080) stays off in this flavour too (round 3 review H1): the module has a bus alias
# (ps3:13:0), so udev would load it at every boot and open the dispatcher manager's vuart, which carries the
# update manager (decision of 2026-10-18, docs/OTHEROS-PATCHES.md). If a research session ever needs it,
# it gets a never-published variant like lockdep, with the module blacklisted.
# package.conf REQUIRE_SET_debug / REQUIRE_UNSET_release keep this split from drifting.
CONFIG_PS3_LV1CALL=m
CONFIG_PS3_PHYSMEM=m
